id: jacket
name: Jacket
kind: crafting
categories: standard-clothing
# "Quality Slots: 1~3" - which, asked when it is added.
slots: 1~3
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Soak Value 1(bT) higher for each Slot it takes, and it can go on over Armor.
# What it does, for the Effects on its Item's sheet: its Effects line as printed, word for
# word, cut into one line to an effect, each opening with its tag as the rulebook writes one.
summary: >
  [Passive]: Increase your Soak Value by x(bT), where x is equal to the number of Quality Slots
  this Apparel Quality is occupying.

  [Passive]: Additionally, this piece of Apparel can be worn over Armor.
text: >
  Jacket: A piece of clothing designed to protect another piece of clothing underneath.
  –Apparel Category: Standard Clothing
  –Prerequisites: N/A
  –Quality Slots: 1~3
  –Effects: Increase your Soak Value by x(bT), where x is equal to the number of Quality Slots this
  Apparel Quality is occupying. Additionally, this piece of Apparel can be worn over Armor.

---

# The Soak Value is the wearer's, while worn: 1(bT) for each Slot. Going on over Armor: while Armor
# is worn nothing goes on but this, and it goes on top of the Armor - equipPlan() in module/gear.mjs.
[passive]
soakValue += 1(bT) * $slots;
piece.wornOverArmor = true;
